"""Publish a local v2 train-only build tree to s3://veox-jopedime-learning-use2/experiments/gp-policy-dl/v2-trainonly/.

Owner decision L6(e): create-only, <= 40e9 bytes in total, never overwrite or delete anything, v1 untouched; TabPFN 3.5
outputs only under v2-trainonly/research-only/ (never readable by the production loader, s3io.assert_production_loadable).

Input: BUILD/shard-*/<view_id>/ as written by tools/v2_build_local.py: context.json (schema jope.dl-v2-local-context/v1,
published=false, files {name: {sha256, bytes}}) and .done. Every listed file maps to one component (FILES below):

  object   v2-trainonly/<sub><dataset_hash>/f<fold>/<split12>-<scaler12>-<code12>.<ext>
  receipt  v2-trainonly/receipts/<component>/<dataset_hash>/f<fold>/<split12>-<scaler12>-<code12>.json
           (tabpfn35: v2-trainonly/research-only/receipts/tabpfn35/...; nothing of it lands outside research-only/)
  split12 = outer_train_indices_sha256[:12], scaler12 = scaler_sha256[:12], code12 = sha256(canonical(code_sha256))[:12]

Every PUT is s3io.put_create_only on a v2 writer (IfNoneMatch='*', ChecksumSHA256, the persisted v2 byte-budget ledger)
followed by an exact-version GET whose sha256 and bytes must match. Receipts are deterministic (context.json fields and
the object's VersionId; no clock), so a resumed run renders identical bytes.

Resumable: a local per-object publish ledger (append-only JSONL, fsynced) records intent before each PUT and the verified
VersionId after its readback. An object already verified there is checked again by an exact-version GET and never
re-put; an interrupted PUT is retried create-only, where a 412 with equal bytes is accepted only after an exact-version
readback. A context is refused before any PUT of it when .done is missing, context.json says published != false or is
malformed, a listed file is unknown, missing, a symlink, or does not hash/size as recorded, an unlisted file sits beside
it, or its key collides with another context's. The build tree is only read, never modified.

--dry-run runs the same code against an in-memory fake bucket that applies the real s3io.Guard at the parameter and
request stages (a v2 writer charged to a COPY of the real budget ledger): no AWS client is built, nothing leaves the host,
and the real publish and budget ledgers are not touched. --real publishes with the guarded boto3 clients (AWS_PROFILE).

Usage (lane slice; see the module report for full command lines):
  v2_publish.py --build RUN/build-v2/L7b --dry-run [--limit N] [--workers N]
  v2_publish.py --build RUN/build-v2/L7b --real    [--limit N] [--workers N]
"""
